## Interface: 50504
## Title: Laurels
## Notes: Custom RP achievements, titles, and rival challenges.
## Author: charl
## Version: 0.2.0
## SavedVariables: LaurelsDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: LaurelsCharDB

# Measured: this client carries SAY/YELL and refuses a custom CHANNEL, the
# exact inverse of WoW-Forever. YELL is therefore the right default here, and
# it restores the proximity "nearby rivals" design. Declaring it per-.toc beats
# sniffing the client at runtime. /deed channel overrides it; the transport
# also falls back on its own if this turns out to be wrong.
## X-BroadcastChannel: YELL

# Mists of Pandaria Classic (live Blizzard realms).
#
# A client picks the .toc matching its flavour and falls back to the plain
# Laurels.toc when there is none, so this file and Laurels.toc coexist:
# MoP Classic reads this one, WoW-Forever reads the other. Keep the file list
# below in sync with Laurels.toc.
#
# ## Interface above is VERIFIED: a live MoP Classic client reports TOC
# version 50504. To re-check after a patch, run in game:
#   /run print(GetBuildInfo())
# and use the LAST value it prints -- NOT the build number. If the addon ever
# shows as out of date, tick "Load out of date AddOns" on the character-select
# AddOns screen, which loads it regardless while you correct this number.

Core.lua
Diagnostics.lua
Tracking\Kinds.lua
Tracking\Signals.lua
Tracking\Engine.lua
Tracking\Sources\KillSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\SwingSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\QuestSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\DeathSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\EmoteSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\SpellSource.lua
Tracking\Sources\FishSource.lua
Rival\Ladder.lua
